<p>Thank you for your fair criticism. Please remember that I am not an expert in these field. That being said I still did some research.</p>
<ul>
<li>You can safely look at SCP, the use of IR/UV-vision is stated in the article and is more accurate/reliable than a normal camera. UV is the most important in my opinion and in terms of research (For decent footage).</li>
</ul>
<ul>
<li>From the image, research that I did, and my own knowledge I didn't know these two types of anechoic chamber could both be described as &quot;anechoic chamber&quot; (I didn't think the acoustic one was called that). I'd say RF seems more accurate here because the SCP doesn't focus on sound.</li>
</ul>
<ul>
<li>From what I can find: the Schrödinger Equation is used to predict light/predict certain probabilities of light (in terms of location and movement). I don't know much about quantum mechanics though. This is one of the preventive measures. Containment isn't only &quot;Yep, we got it locked up&quot; as far as I am concerned. It is a constant process of observation and evaluation, therefore preventive measures are needed.</li>
</ul>
<ul>
<li>The cold is probably fridge logic (or at least what I think you mean by that). The aura's more important ability is that it blurs SCP-5927.</li>
</ul>
<ul>
<li>Bone marrow or medulla ossium is found mostly in bones, ribs, sternum (English word?) and the spine. It is important for a lot of biological processes. This includes the immune/blood- and nervous-system. Neurotransmitters are in the neurons specifically which run through your entire body. Also I could have been more specific about the spinal cord (white/grey matter in the nervous system etc.) but whilst in the drafting phase this made the SCP really long and tedious to read (even for myself). I don't want the reader to look up everything the wouldn't understand, then this would just be a biology lesson.</li>
</ul>
<ul>
<li>Didn't know that about glass.</li>
</ul>
<ul>
<li>The radioisotopes are just help the foundation keep track of how much phosphate (weakening factor) is in the prism left. The tracking can be done via radiation, which I believe radioisotopes give (perhaps over time). Not going to lie this was hard to look up in my own language and I might have misinterpreted it in English, so I can see this being a plothole.</li>
</ul>
<p>To clarify; this was a quick reply. I hope this was helpful.</p>

