<p>Greetings. Let me start by saying that i really liked this entity and the clever way of its containment, i think this is a good scp, altough i do thing it has some rough spots, mainly on the ammount of wording you use in some parts.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Leaving aside the fact that this is supposed to be a report on SCP-5927 and its containment, repeating its scp number on the description could get a little repetive, as its basically its name, repeating your &quot;main character's&quot; name over and over on a story is not ussually a good thing, maybe change some of them to &quot;the entity&quot; or &quot;it&quot; would be great.</p>
<p>I dont want to say much about the failed Containment Attempts as i cant point out a good way to &quot;improve&quot; on them, but i feel them much like padding, having even an Einstein's quote on there doesnt really tell me much as a reader, and its ok if you like them there, but i felt the need to skip the failed attempts alltogether (although i did read them and i can say that i can see the positives on letting us know more about the R&amp;D of the contaiment, but it felt more like a youtube tutorial)</p>
<p>Getting into the Flare incident report i found details like</p>
<div class="code">
<pre>
<code>SCP-5927 proceeds to absorb their neurotransmitters, killing them</code>
</pre></div>
<br />
as kind of unnecesary information, by this point in the report the reader knows very well what the skip does with its friky light tentacles, might as well feed on them or instantly break their spines, the agents are killed by the entity, i dont think knowing it eat something while killing them tells me anything important
<p>And this last is probably the most subjective but i find it weird that the victim of this SCP is refferd as a PoI and not SCP-5927-1 as most other skips do, i mean, wondertainment is a PoI, a soon-to-be skip brunch is not a person of interest, at least as the foundation is concerned.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>All that aside is a spooky monster being contained in an interesting way so i say this is a good one, i havent yet rated an article but i say you get my first +1 good sir/lady. Have a nice day.</p>

